<header>

<h1>Grants You Didn't Know Existed</h1>

<p>
Most people think grants are only available to nonprofits, researchers,
or large organizations. In reality, grants exist for entrepreneurs,
artists, tradespeople, farmers, community projects, housing assistance,
career training, veterans, women, minorities, inventors, and many others.
This guide is designed to help you discover funding opportunities you may
have never considered.
</p>

<div class="hero-buttons">
<a href="#grants">Explore Grant Types</a>
<a href="#resources">Grant Databases</a>
</div>

</header>

<section class="intro">

<h2>Funding Opportunities Beyond Traditional Loans</h2>

<p>
Unlike loans, grants generally do not need to be repaid. They can help
people start businesses, learn new skills, launch projects, improve their
communities, develop products, create art, purchase equipment, and build
financial independence. Many grant opportunities are overlooked simply
because people never realize they exist.
</p>

</section>

